  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1139 AM CDT Sun Oct 18 2026\n\nCalmer Winds Today, Turning Cloudier:\n\nWhile calmer winds are expected today, cloudier skies are expected \nto affect the local forecast area, building through the daytime \nhours before eventually exiting tonight. The responsible final \nstages of upstream trougholysis advects a band of increased low \nlevel moisture across the forecast area before subsequent \nanticyclonic flow fills in across the Upper Mississippi River \nValley. Have increased daytime high temperatures a couple of degrees \noff of National Blend in collaboration with neighboring forecast \noffices based on forecast trends and recent observations. Resultant \ndaytime highs will feel more like the start of October instead of \nthe penultimate week to the month. \n\nLowering Confidence in Subsequent Precipitation Chances:\n\nA temporary, weak synoptic omega pattern keeps the local \nforecast area in a dry pattern with slightly above normal \ntemperatures through the week. Local precipitation chances this \nweekend are decreasing in confidence due to a stronger solution \nto the upper level ridge through the central CONUS. Resultant \nadvection of the required synoptic forcing lifts farther \nwest/northwest than previous forecasts.",
